# Build output. No leading slash, because each language keeps its build directory inside its
# own subdirectory (Cargo's target/ is under rust/), so one pattern covers any depth and
# adding go/ or js/ later needs no new line.
target/
# A library crate does not commit its lock file, which Cargo recommends since only binaries
# should. If another language has a lock file of its own, list it here for the same reason.
Cargo.lock


# Design drafts, kept outside the repository: this directory is not version controlled, so a
# fresh clone does not have it. Anything in it is disposable, and any conclusion must be
# written into docs/ before it counts for anything.
/prd/

# ==================== Operating systems ====================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ==================== Editors ====================
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.code-workspace